---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "Privacy Policy for MorseCodeGenerator.com. Learn what data we collect, how analytics and ads work, and your choices.";
const canonical = "https://morsecodegenerator.com/privacy/";
const robots = "index,follow";

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "morsecodegenerator@gmail.com";
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "2026-05-15";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} robots={robots}>
  <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a class="crumb" href="/">Home</a>
    <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
    <span class="crumb-current">Privacy</span>
  </nav>

  <article class="prose">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="page-hero-kicker">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="muted page-hero-sub">
        How MorseCodeGenerator.com handles information when you use the site.
      </p>
    </header>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>MorseCodeGenerator.com</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”) handles information
      when you use this website (the “Service”).
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Quick summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The translator runs locally in your browser. We do not require accounts or logins to use the tool.
      </li>
      <li>
        We use analytics (Google Analytics 4) to understand general usage (for example, which pages are popular).
      </li>
      <li>
        We may show ads (Google AdSense). Ads and analytics may use cookies or similar identifiers depending on your settings and region.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can control cookies/ads via your browser settings and Google’s ad/analytics controls.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>Information we process</h2>

    <h3>1) Information you provide</h3>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email, you provide your email address and the content of your message. We use it only to respond.
      Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>2) Usage data (analytics)</h3>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong> to measure and improve the Service. GA4 may collect information such as:
      page views, approximate location, device/browser information, and interaction events. We configure GA4 with IP anonymization
      (where supported) to reduce identifiability.
    </p>

    <h3>3) Advertising data (AdSense)</h3>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to display ads. AdSense may use cookies or similar technologies to show ads and measure
      performance. Depending on your region and settings, Google may serve personalized or non-personalized ads.
    </p>

    <h3>4) Translator input</h3>
    <p>
      The translator runs in your browser. We do not intentionally collect the text you type into the translator through the website’s
      own servers. However, remember that your browser, extensions, operating system, or third-party scripts may still have access to what
      you type.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small files stored by your browser. Analytics and advertising providers may use cookies, local storage, or similar
      identifiers for measurement, fraud prevention, and ad delivery.
    </p>

    <h3>Cookie consent banner</h3>
    <p>
      On your first visit you'll see a banner asking you to choose between
      <strong>Accept all</strong> (analytics + ads enabled) and
      <strong>Essential only</strong> (no analytics, no ads loaded). Your
      choice is stored locally as <code>mcg-consent</code> in your
      browser's <code>localStorage</code> — not in a server-side cookie —
      and is honoured on every subsequent page load.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change your decision at any time by clicking
      <a href="#" data-open-consent>Cookie preferences</a> in the site
      footer. Switching from "Accept all" back to "Essential only" stops
      analytics and ad scripts from being loaded on the next pageview;
      already-loaded scripts may persist in the current tab until you
      reload. Clearing your browser's site data will also clear your
      preference (the banner will reappear).
    </p>

    <h3>Funding & disclosure</h3>
    <p>
      For a plain-English breakdown of how this site is funded — ads,
      affiliate links, reader support — see the
      <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Browser controls:</strong> You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Some site functionality may be affected.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google ad controls:</strong> You can manage ad personalization in your Google account settings (if applicable).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics controls:</strong> Google provides tools and settings to control analytics collection (availability depends on region/device).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Do Not Track:</strong> Some browsers offer “Do Not Track” signals. There is no universal standard; we do not guarantee a specific response.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Operate and maintain the Service</li>
      <li>Understand what content is helpful and improve pages/features</li>
      <li>Detect abuse, security issues, or fraud (including via third parties like Google)</li>
      <li>Respond to inquiries you send us</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we share information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We may share information in these cases:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service providers:</strong> Analytics and ads providers (e.g., Google) process usage data to provide their services.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal:</strong> If required by law or to protect rights, safety, and security.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Business changes:</strong> If the site is transferred, information may be transferred as part of that change.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Email messages are kept as long as needed to respond and maintain reasonable records. Analytics and ad data retention is controlled by
      the relevant providers and their settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not intended for children under 13 (or the relevant minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect
      personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>International visitors</h2>
    <p>
      If you access the site from outside the country where hosting or providers operate, your data may be processed in other countries.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Effective date” above indicates the most recent revision.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions? Email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
